    "case_summary": "In July 2002, a 42-year-old male weighing 230 pounds was admitted to a peripheral community hospital presenting with fever, chills, and malaise, which began 7-10 days following a visit to a local beach. He was treated for community-acquired left lower lobe pneumonia with three different antibiotics. Despite treatment, he continued to have a fever with temperatures ranging from 39 to 40 degrees Celsius. Ten days after his initial admission, he was transferred to our hospital.\n\nThe wet preparation showed budding yeast.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n",
